stremio-server-installer for Debian
====================================

What this package is
---------------------

`server.js` is Stremio's proprietary streaming server component. Stremio's
own dev lead has stated it is "not meant to be used / distributed outside
of an official Stremio app" (see
https://github.com/Stremio/stremio-shell/issues/435), and no explicit
grant permitting Debian to redistribute copies of it through Debian's own
mirrors has been obtained. It is therefore not included in this package,
and this package is not itself proprietary or non-free software.

Instead, this package's `postinst` downloads server.js directly from
Stremio's own CDN (the same public URL Stremio's own official downloads
use) onto the user's own machine at install time, verifies its checksum,
and installs it to `/usr/share/stremio/server.js` (where the `stremio`
package's wrapper script expects it via `SERVER_PATH`). Debian never
hosts or redistributes the file itself.

This is the same model used by two real, currently-shipping Debian
`contrib` packages facing an equivalent problem:

- `ttf-mscorefonts-installer` (Microsoft's TrueType fonts)
- `virtualbox-ext-pack` (Oracle's proprietary, PUEL-licensed VirtualBox
  Extension Pack)

`debian/postinst.in`/`debian/rules`/`debian/templates`/`debian/config`
are modeled directly on `virtualbox-ext-pack`'s real packaging
(`https://salsa.debian.org/pkg-virtualbox-team/virtualbox-ext-pack`).

Updating to a new server.js release
------------------------------------

This is a Debian-native package (`3.0 (native)`): its own version number
(`debian/changelog`) is just this package's own release counter and is
independent of which server.js version it fetches.

1. Download the new `https://dl.strem.io/server/v<version>/desktop/server.js`
   and compute its real sha256sum.
2. Update `SERVER_VERSION` and `SERVER_SHA256` in `debian/rules` to match.
3. Add a `debian/changelog` entry describing the server.js version bump
   (bumping this package's own native version, e.g. 1 -> 2).

Do not bump `SERVER_VERSION`/`SERVER_SHA256` without actually downloading
and hashing the real file for that version.
